// ── Module 23: Library Management ─────────────────────────────────────

/// The physical life of one copy. AVAILABLE/ISSUED/RESERVED are the
/// circulating states; LOST/DAMAGED/WITHDRAWN are terminal and drop the
/// copy out of stock counts (roadmap §6) without deleting the row —
/// "we used to own this" is a fact a stock report has to be able to say.
enum BookCopyStatus {
  AVAILABLE
  ISSUED
  RESERVED
  LOST
  DAMAGED
  WITHDRAWN

  @@map("book_copy_status_enum")
}

/// A copy's physical condition, recorded when it is added and again on
/// every return. An enum rather than free text because roadmap §8's
/// damaged-on-return dispute needs the *change* between the two to be
/// comparable — a note beside it carries the argument.
enum BookCondition {
  NEW
  GOOD
  FAIR
  POOR
  DAMAGED

  @@map("book_condition_enum")
}

/// Who holds the card. Polymorphic over `students`, `teachers` and
/// `staff_profiles` with no FK — the M12 `staff_attendances` / M21
/// `leave_applications` precedent, because the three tables share no
/// supertype and a library card is issued to a *person*, not to a role.
enum LibraryMemberType {
  STUDENT
  TEACHER
  STAFF

  @@map("library_member_type_enum")
}

/// ACTIVE borrows; SUSPENDED keeps the history and the outstanding
/// loans while refusing new ones (what a school does about repeated
/// damage); CLOSED is the card handed back on the way out.
enum LibraryMemberStatus {
  ACTIVE
  SUSPENDED
  CLOSED

  @@map("library_member_status_enum")
}

/// Why money is owed on a loan. Stored rather than inferred from the
/// dates, because a lost book charged at replacement price and an
/// overdue book charged per day are different lines in the income
/// report, and a copy marked lost after being returned late is both.
enum LibraryFineReason {
  NONE
  OVERDUE
  LOST
  DAMAGED

  @@map("library_fine_reason_enum")
}

/// A hold on a *title*, not on a copy — a member wants the book, any
/// copy of it. Roadmap §3 put `RESERVED` in the copy-status enum and §4
